The literal complete finite old H is unchanged. Its supplied simple spectrum, distinct positive gaps, a designated local Hermitian B with every off-diagonal energy-basis transition nonzero, computable spectral data and vacant exterior geometry are additional hypotheses. A generic augmented Lie certificate has not been shown to imply them. The source states, reference time, continued isolation and calibrated coefficients are supplied. All old, bus and source outputs, arbitrary passive references, actual runtime and reserve phases remain in the output statement.

The positive-cone core, routed tree, complete Q/P spectral separation, SU(2) resolvent, quadratic source counterterms, connected-resonance classification, finite Sylvester correctors and actual-time phases were completely read by root. Full many-body separation uses the zero-route spectrum and full-space perturbation bound, not false subset-sum diagonalization of a branched XY bus. The counterterms act on the complete source space, including off-code sectors. Actual positive reserve R, normalized trace scalar and source phases at T are distinct and retained. The resulting J_*=R_s+7M_E+2/t_* bounds incident interaction strength on this conditional domain; it gives no favorable runtime, coefficient precision, global norm or efficient search bound.

Exact-target existence may use specified support and phases for a fixed L. The assertion that arbitrary computable L automatically permits exact zero/support decisions or arg(L_ab) is not accepted. The separately root-proposed, exposed-review-checked effective repair is: approximate L in the supplied old eigenbasis by rational Hermitian M with ||M-L||<=epsilon/32; entry accuracy epsilon/(32d) suffices. Its support is decidable; zero entries have r_l=0 and phase1. Nonzero entries use the computable unit phase (M_ab/|M_ab|)(conj(kappa_ab)/|kappa_ab|)exp(i omega_l T). Run the construction for M at epsilon/2, including its correspondingly reduced preparation and integrated perturbation budgets. The full trace allowance is then epsilon/2+2||M-L||<=9epsilon/16. The old spectral boxes and hardware ceiling depend on fixed H,B,t_*, not on M; target-dependent loads are absorbed into positive xi-smallness. Certified upper rounding selects N with bounded additive excess, and strict positive searches avoid undecidable boundary tests. Preserve this repair as an attributed added argument, not an unnoticed edit to the author proof.

Root read both successful author science sources, exact failed-to-success changes and all four launches, results and full streams. Two original failed launcher versions are missing; current launchers and retained main-source captures do not recover those missing bytes. The author's finite tests include one full512-dimensional fixture and a30-dimensional one-particle routed bus, not the full many-body30-site controller.

